\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces Phoenix trace of the Review~3 misread walkthrough (synthetic pack, hybrid planner). (1)~trace latency 8.8\,s and cost \$0 (local model); (2)~root \texttt {check} span of kind \textsc {agent}; (3)~branch point after the empty exact search, where the model chose \texttt {search\_variants} (4.6\,s); (4)~branch point after grading, where the model chose \texttt {ask\_user} (3.9\,s); (5)~the resumed half of the check under the same root; (6)~the input fields, with the batch read by OCR as \texttt {LM24088}; (7)~the check pauses with a \texttt {confirm\_char} question that offers \texttt {LM24088} and \texttt {LM2408B}.}}{36}{figure.caption.46}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.2}{\ignorespaces Correct verdicts per scenario on seed~7 with a person answering ($n=8$ per scenario, 4 for siblings). ``Not listed'' denotes the not-listed control packs. The baseline fails on the misread, collision and sibling packs.}}{40}{figure.caption.50}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.3}{\ignorespaces Effect of the human answer for the agent with the rule planner, seed~7. Without answers the agent abstains (\textsc {cant\_verify}) on 36 of 60 packs, so hit recall falls while the false-alarm rate stays at zero.}}{40}{figure.caption.51}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.4}{\ignorespaces Time per pack on seed~7 ($n=60$, oracle). Left: end-to-end time (shared perception plus reasoning). Right: reasoning time only. Solid bars are medians and hatched bars 95th percentiles. The hybrid planner's local model calls set its tail.}}{41}{figure.caption.52}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.1}{\ignorespaces Headline metrics on the development set (seed~1) and the evaluation set (seed~7), a person answering, $n=60$ each. Labels give $k/n$ and whiskers are Wilson 95\% intervals. The agent arms give the same counts on both sets; the lookup differs by one pack.}}{45}{figure.caption.60}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.2}{\ignorespaces Agent with the rule planner on seed~7 before (run~1) and after the three D25 fixes (run~2), a person answering. Left: rates with Wilson 95\% intervals. Right: correct verdicts per scenario. Run~1 is reported in full; because the fixes were made after it, run~2 is not a blind test.}}{46}{figure.caption.62}%
